Build aarch64 Windows natively rather than cross-compiling

windows-11-arm has been free for public repositories since the arm64
runners entered public preview, but ci-runners.yaml still marks it
free: false. find_runner is called with free=True for Windows, so it
finds no aarch64 match, falls back to the first free Windows runner,
and every aarch64 target is cross-compiled from x64 through
vcvarsamd64_arm64.bat.

Correcting the flag lets find_runner match on architecture, so those
targets build on a native arm64 runner instead.

diff --git a/ci-runners.yaml b/ci-runners.yaml
index e6bdd0f..5df0948 100644
--- a/ci-runners.yaml
+++ b/ci-runners.yaml
@@ -45,7 +45,9 @@ windows-2025-vs2026:
   platform: windows
   free: true
 
+# Free for public repositories since the arm64 runners entered public
+# preview: https://github.com/orgs/community/discussions/155713
 windows-11-arm:
   arch: aarch64
   platform: windows
-  free: false
+  free: true
